**Test filters.** For this step these gates run only the tests their filter selects (plus any inherited expected-red tests); put the tests this step adds or changes where a filter value finds them:
- `ui-smoke`: 
- `ui-tests`: `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ImportDialogTests`, `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ScrollExtentTests`

**How to implement.** The import dialog's window, and the one drop seam of the library windows (the S3.2 brief: a new window with its own view and window files; 001 §H; .spec-md §4 'UI': every new window calls `WindowFit.keepOnScreen` and joins `ScrollExtentTests`). (1) New `OpticalConstructor.Ui/ImportDialogWindow.fs` in `namespace OpticalConstructor.Ui`, compiled directly after `ImportDialogView.fs`, one `<Compile>` line and no comment. (a) `type ImportDialogWindow(imports : CatalogueImportContext, request : ImportDialogRequest, onApplied : ImportDialogApplied -> unit)` inherits `HostWindow`, as `MaterialsWindow` (`MaterialsWindow.fs:29`) does. Its title is `Import decisions`; its `Name` and `AutomationId` are `ConstructorUiId.importDialogWindow`; it asks for 900 × 640 and then calls `WindowFit.keepOnScreen this` (`OpticalConstructor.Controls/WindowLayout.fs:WindowFit.keepOnScreen`). It runs `Program.mkProgram` over `initImportDialog`, `updateImportDialog` and `importDialogView` (step 107) with the context `{ imports = imports; request = request; onApplied = onApplied; requestClose = this.Close }`. Closing it any other way than Apply applies nothing, because only `ApplyImportChoices` reaches the seam. Its doc is one to three lines citing 001 §B and spec 0050 S3.2. (b) `module EntryFileDrop` holds `acceptEntryFiles (window : Window) (onDropped : FileName list -> unit) : unit`, the one drop seam of the Library and Materials windows (001 §H). It calls `DragDrop.SetAllowDrop(window, true)` and adds two handlers through `DragDrop.AddDragOverHandler` and `DragDrop.AddDropHandler`. The drag-over handler sets `e.DragEffects` to `DragDropEffects.Copy` when `e.DataTransfer.Contains DataFormat.File`, and to `DragDropEffects.None` otherwise. The drop handler takes `e.DataTransfer.TryGetFiles ()` and calls `onDropped` with each item's `Path.LocalPath` as a `FileName`, in order, when there is at least one. It is an IO edge in the shape of `TableAndElementRotationView.fs:pickDataFile`: each handler body is wrapped so that a platform failure changes nothing, and headless facts send the windows' drop message directly (steps 110, 111). Its doc is one to three lines. (2) `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/ScrollExtentTests.fs` gains `the import dialog leaves everything reachable`: `assertReachable "ImportDialog"` over an `ImportDialogWindow` whose request is `ApplyDroppedEntries` of one `EntryIdNotHeld` row per envelope of `BuiltinCatalogue.catalogueData ()`, each `ImportDecision.decide (DroppedFileOrigin <its file name>) envelope None []`, and one `NameCollision` row against two same-name held entries, so the list is longer than the screen and one row's options are wide. Its import context is `CatalogueImportContext.create (CatalogueImportProxy.createInMemory ()).proxy`, and `onApplied` is `ignore`. (3) `ImportDialogTests` gains `acceptance: the import dialog window renders its rows with Apply and Cancel in one row, and Apply imports the chosen entries and closes it` (trait `ui-smoke`). Over the class's in-memory context and two dropped rows (step 107), an `ImportDialogWindow` with a recording `onApplied` is shown headless. It shows `importDialogHeading`, `importDecisionList` holding both rows, and `importApplyButton` and `importCancelButton` with equal tops, Cancel to the right of Apply with a gap between them. Pressing Apply's centre, as the file's other facts press a box, holds both entries, records one `onApplied`, and closes the window.

**Acceptance.** After the window lands, `ImportDialogWindow` MUST call `WindowFit.keepOnScreen`, and `EntryFileDrop.acceptEntryFiles` MUST be the one drop seam; ui-smoke MUST pass, including `acceptance: the import dialog window renders its rows with Apply and Cancel in one row, and Apply imports the chosen entries and closes it`, the count rising by 1; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, including `the import dialog leaves everything reachable`, the count rising by 1; and build, elevation and the eleven s13 invariants MUST pass.
